[task-01] Model calls move from OpenAI to Claude. The default model becomes
    `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5`, and the summary-span stage, which today names
    `openai/gpt-5.4` as its own model, runs on the default like every other stage.
    -> model-calls-move-to-claude  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Model calls move from OpenAI to Claude.
    -> default-model-anthropic-claude-sonnet-5-5  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Set the default model to `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5`.
    -> summary-span-uses-default-model  [compatibility/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The summary-span stage runs on the default model like every other stage.

[task-02] Claude accepts neither a seed nor a temperature, so a run against it is
    reproducible only through its recorded transcripts. A recorded Claude run replays
    with no live call, and two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical
    review state. The run still requests temperature 0 and seed 0, and the review's
    provenance records that Claude applied neither. The module documentation states this
    as the determinism strategy for Claude.
    -> claude-accepts-neither-seed-nor-temperature  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Claude accepts neither a seed nor a temperature.
    -> recorded-transcripts-reproducibility  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A run against Claude is reproducible only through its recorded transcripts.
    -> recorded-run-replays-no-live-call  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A recorded Claude run replays with no live call.
    -> byte-identical-review-state  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review state.
    -> request-temperature-zero-and-seed-zero  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The run requests temperature 0 and seed 0.
    -> provenance-records-claude-applied-neither  [docs_config/explicit, code_only]
       The review's provenance records that Claude applied neither.
       why code_only: This is a provenance/documentation record in the review metadata,
       which is settled by the recorded output itself rather than by runtime behavior or
       a test.
    -> doc-determinism-strategy-for-claude  [docs_config/explicit, code_only]
       Document that the determinism strategy for Claude is to rely on recorded
       transcripts because Claude accepts neither a seed nor a temperature.
       why code_only: This requirement is satisfied by the module documentation text
       itself; no runtime behavior or test is needed to establish that the documentation
       states the strategy.

